.Dd August 12, 2026
.Dt MOUNT_VIRTIOFS 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm mount_virtiofs
.Nd mount a virtio-fs shared directory
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl o Ar options
.Ar tag | special
.Ar node
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility attaches a
.Em virtio-fs
shared directory exported by the hypervisor to the file system.
.Pp
virtio-fs is the FUSE protocol carried over VirtIO request queues.
The
.Xr virtio_fs 4
guest driver publishes one
.Pa /dev/virtiofs Ns Ar N
character device per virtio-fs PCI function and drives an in-kernel FUSE
session over the device queues, so the mounted file system is of type
.Xr fusefs 5 .
.Pp
The first argument is either the mount
.Ar tag
configured on the host (resolved to the matching device through the
.Va dev.virtio_fs. Ns Ar N Ns Va .tag
sysctl), or an explicit device node path beginning with
.Ql / .
The second argument is the mount point.
.Pp
The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl o Ar options
Options are passed to
.Xr nmount 2 .
In addition to the standard file system options described in
.Xr mount 8 ,
the fusefs flag options
.Cm allow_other , default_permissions , intr , push_symlinks_in
and
.Cm auto_unmount
are recognised, along with
.Cm max_read Ns = Ns Ar n .
.El
.Pp
Unless overridden,
.Nm
bounds
.Cm max_read
to 131072 bytes so that each FUSE read fits in a single transport request.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr nmount 2 ,
.Xr virtio_fs 4 ,
.Xr fusefs 5 ,
.Xr mount 8 ,
.Xr mount_fusefs 8
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
utility first appeared as part of the 5BSD virtio-fs guest driver.
.Sh CAVEATS
This is a first-slice implementation.
DAX, the notification queue, and packed rings are not yet negotiated.
